  "title": "Rentals.ca Yaletown Vancouver Apartments, Condos and Houses For Rent",
  "bodyText": "Landlords\nRent Report\nBlog\nLogin\nEN\nFR\nPost a Rental\nPost a Rental\nLogin\nCreate Account\nAlerts\nFAQs\nMonthly Rent Report\nCity Rent Trends\nLandlords\nCredit Reports\nCommercial Properties\nRaising the Roof\nCareers\nAbout\nBlog\n Contact us\n Instagram\n Facebook\n Youtube\n LinkedIn\n X\n TikTok\nNearby Places\nPrice\nType\nBeds\nFilters\nList\nSplit\nMap\n2\n2\n2\n2\n2\n2\n2\n2\n4\n4\n3\n2\n3\n2\n2\n2\n2\n2\n2\n2\n$1995+\n$2159+\n$1+\n$1650+\n$1+\n$2164\n$2295\n$1990+\n$1999\n$2564+\n+\n−\nKeyboard shortcuts\nMap data ©2026 Google\n200 m \nTerms\nReport a map error\nHome\nBC\nVancouver\nYaletown\nYaletown Vancouver Apartments, Condos and Houses for Rent\n\n5 Rentals found \n\nSort\nDefault\nRecent\nPrice - $\nPrice - $$$\n\nRent Guide\n\nPromoted\n1 / 32\nContact\n\n$2595\n\nCondo\n\n Verified\n1 BED\n1 BATH\n609 FT²\n928 Beatty Street, Vancouver, BC\n\n$2800\n\nCondo\n\n Verified\n1 BED\n1 BATH\n610 FT²\n002 - 1212 Howe St, Vancouver, BC\n\n$5250\n\nCondo\n\n Verified\n2 BED\n2 BATH\n1455 Howe St, Vancouver, BC\n\n$3900\n\nCondo\n\n Verified\n1 BED\n1 BATH\n590 FT²\n1372 Seymour St, Vancouver, BC\n\n$3695\n\nCondo\n\n Verified\n2 BED\n2 BATH\n800 FT²\n603 - 189 Davie Street, Vancouver, BC\nYaletown, BC\n\nRenting Guide\n\nAbout\nRental Options\nLife & Style\nNeighbourhood\nLand Mark\nFun Fact\nTrendy, Industrial-Chic Downtown Living\nAbout\n\nInto history, but in that sort of modern, trendy hipster way? You’re meant to be a Yaletownie! One of the most desirable locales in the city, Yaletown has a ton of historical interest, but it’s channeled through a modern lens. That’s why it’s the epitome of hipster culture. Just like hipster culture, the neighbourhood has a sort of intense, sort of laid back vibe. If that sounds like your kind of place, throw Yaletown on your vision board, buy your moustache wax, and get your Insta game on fleek. Oh and get a bad ass job with a big paycheque because Yaletown has some of the highest rents in all of Vancouver!\n\nRental Options\n\nThe Market\n\nAvg. rent by housing size\n\nBach/studio: $2,026\n\n1-bedroom: $2,300\n\n2-bedroom: $4,688\n\n3-bedroom: $5,745\n\nAvg. rent compared to other Canadian cities\n\nYaletown is 101% higher than the Canadian average\n\nYaletown Rental Market: Yaletown aparments for rent are made up of mainly apartment buildings and condos. Prices have sky-rocketed, pushing a lot of people out of the area. While there are attempts to bring some affordable housing units into the neighbourhood, most of the buildings cater to young people with money. There are gyms, pools, and 24-hour concierge desks in most buildings. Studios and one-bedrooms are priced just about the same, since trendy, renovated lofts make up some of the most desirable units in this neighbourhood.\n\nApartment Hunting in Yaletown: Yaletown apartments for rent and condos for rent may not be cheap rentals, but that doesn’t mean they’re all full-on luxury. There are some high-end condo buildings that cater to singles and couples with studios and one-bedrooms. Older apartment buildings have fewer amenities, but also tend to have a greater variety of prices and sizes, including two-bedrooms and three-bedrooms. In all, just be careful that you are getting enough for the money you’re spending.\n\nTypical housing type: High-rises and condos.\n\nLife & Style\n\nLife in Yaletown revolves around what’s new and next. Since locals tend to be singles or young couples, they love going out and having fun. Here, it’s more about going to see cool indie bands or checking out the latest interesting theme bar. Locals also tend to have jobs with flexible schedules so they can hang out in the daytime too, working whenever and wherever they feel like it. It’s that blend of hard work and fun that gives Yaletown its hipster feel.\n\nNeighbourhood\n\nFor public transit, Yaletown-Roundhouse station connects Yaletown to the rest of Vancouver by SkyTrain. Buses run on Pacific Street as well. At the bottom of the neighbourhood is the Roundhouse Community Arts and Recreation Centre, a liquor store, and an Urban Fare grocery store. The core of the neighbourhood is filled with various restaurants and bars, especially on Mainland and Hamilton Streets. Just outside the neighbourhood are several parks, as well as BC Place.\n\nLand Mark\n\nRoundhouse Community Arts and Recreation Centre\n\nYaletown Park\n\nFun Fact\n\nYaletown has a reputation for being a celebrity go-to for dining and nightlife. From sushi to Cioppino’s, Yaletown’s restaurants draw actors, singers, athletes, and more. If celeb spotting is part of why you want to live in the area, your best bet is to hit the hot dining spots and bars during the Vancouver International Film Festival.\n\nHome\nBC\nVancouver\nYaletown\n Back to top\nBlog\nPress\nContact\nAbout\nCareers\nFAQs\nTerms\nPrivacy Policy\nSitemap\nPopular Searches\nApartments Near Me\nCondos Near Me\nHouses Near Me\nRooms Near Me\nPopular Cities\nToronto Rentals\nCalgary Rentals\nOttawa Rentals\nEdmonton Rentals\nVancouver Rentals\nHalifax Rentals\nPopular Provinces\nOntario\nBritish Columbia\nAlberta\nQuebec\nNova Scotia\nManitoba\nLandlords\nGet Listed\nMy Listings\nTenant Credit Check\nResources\nRent Report\nCity Rent Trends\nCommercial Properties\nGet the Rentals.ca app\nProud partner of\n\nCopyright © 2026 Rentals.ca Network, Inc. All rights reserved.\n\nManage Cookies\n \nThis website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience on our website. By clicking \"Allow All\", you consent to our use of cookies. Privacy Policy ↗\nManage Cookies\nDecline\nAllow All",
